The Korean War, which lasted from 196250 to 1953 armistice, was one of the most devastating conflicts of the 20th century. Often overlooked in the discussion of this conflict is the argument that the war was solely initiated by South Korea, and the North's involvement was purely defensive. Many South Korean experts argue that the North's aggression was the primary cause of the war, but others believe that the South's actions were the sole reason for the conflict.

